From: Nguyen Phan <nguyen@nguyenphan.org>
Date: Mon, 10 Nov 2026 20:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] server: /snapshot, one document for the engine's sessions

The dashboard needed a compiled gauge per question — pool rows, chunk speed, conversation ids,
per-stream progress — which cost ten engine rebuilds in one night (2026-11-04). /snapshot is the
interface instead: one document, one timestamp, and new facts are consumer-side work.

- streams[] is the session spine: `slot` is stable for the request's life, so a series can never
  switch conversation between scrapes; the request's own facts (prompt, cached, context, generated)
  travel with it, as does the position of its prompt pass when it is the one filling.
- why requests wait, counted where each hold is decided: the single "waiting" number hid six
  reasons, and requests that gave their lane back for room (ContextFull) were published as a hard
  zero.
- the prompt cache's memory tier (bytes it may hold, and how much is spare), the conversations the
  store knows, and the pool's kept rows by conversation.

Session-level facts leave /metrics (it keeps the counters and the pair families): a gauge per
question is what made the rebuilds necessary. The route joins the status allowlist in auth.zig,
beside /metrics, /stats and /dashboard.
